WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.257
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:08.955
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.255 --> 00:00:15.600
Unit thirty-eight: Can, Could and May (requests). Today you will ask for things and permission politely.

4
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.552
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.988
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:24.572
Can I...?.

7
00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:28.863
Can I...? means a common way to ask permission.

8
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:30.776
Can I open the window?

9
00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:33.885
Your turn. Say: Can I...?.

10
00:00:36.733 --> 00:00:37.525
Can I...?.

11
00:00:38.283 --> 00:00:39.075
Could you...?.

12
00:00:40.083 --> 00:00:43.955
Could you...? means a polite way to ask someone to do something.

13
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:45.795
Could you help me?

14
00:00:46.383 --> 00:00:48.792
Your turn. Say: Could you...?.

15
00:00:51.633 --> 00:00:52.391
Could you...?.

16
00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:54.116
May I...?.

17
00:00:55.117 --> 00:00:58.315
May I...? means a formal way to ask permission.

18
00:00:58.917 --> 00:01:00.150
May I come in?

19
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.996
Your turn. Say: May I...?.

20
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:06.800
May I...?.

21
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:08.354
Please.

22
00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.953
Please means a polite word for requests.

23
00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:13.946
Could you wait, please?

24
00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.156
Your turn. Say: Please.

25
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:20.839
Please.

26
00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:22.387
Sure.

27
00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.975
Sure means a friendly word that means yes.

28
00:01:26.583 --> 00:01:28.060
Sure, no problem.

29
00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:31.070
Your turn. Say: Sure.

30
00:01:33.933 --> 00:01:34.853
Sure.

31
00:01:35.617 --> 00:01:36.862
Sorry, I can't.

32
00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:40.337
Sorry, I can't means a polite way to say no.

33
00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.822
Sorry, I can't help today.

34
00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:46.034
Your turn. Say: Sorry, I can't.

35
00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.273
Sorry, I can't.

36
00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:51.971
Request.

37
00:01:52.983 --> 00:01:55.819
Request means a polite way of asking for something.

38
00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:58.080
A request is a question.

39
00:01:58.683 --> 00:02:00.941
Your turn. Say: Request.

40
00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:04.720
Request.

41
00:02:05.483 --> 00:02:06.426
Permission.

42
00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:10.333
Permission means a yes from someone who is in charge.

43
00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.532
I asked for permission.

44
00:02:13.117 --> 00:02:15.548
Your turn. Say: Permission.

45
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.215
Permission.

46
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.744
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:27.990
Visal, you need to leave the room. What do you ask the teacher?

48
00:02:29.083 --> 00:02:37.880
May I go out, please? We use may, can and could to ask permission or to request. May I and could you are more polite than can I.

49
00:02:38.983 --> 00:02:40.321
What is the difference?

50
00:02:41.417 --> 00:02:52.883
Can I open the window? It is normal and friendly. Could you help me? It is polite. May I come in? It is the most formal. The verb after them is always the base verb.

51
00:02:53.983 --> 00:02:55.205
How do we reply?

52
00:02:56.317 --> 00:03:09.350
To agree: Sure. Of course. Yes, you can. To refuse: Sorry, I can't. Sorry, not now. We always say thank you after a favour. It keeps our request kind.

53
00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.024
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:12.883 --> 00:03:18.517
Grammar focus: Requests: Can and Could and May plus subject plus base verb.

55
00:03:18.817 --> 00:03:19.992
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:20.683 --> 00:03:22.079
Can I open the window?

57
00:03:22.983 --> 00:03:24.704
Could you help me, please?

58
00:03:25.617 --> 00:03:26.757
May I come in?

59
00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:35.475
Use can, could and may to request or ask permission. May I and Could you are more polite than Can I. After them, use the base verb.

60
00:03:36.217 --> 00:03:39.333
Be careful! Don't say: Could you to help me?

61
00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.416
Say: Could you help me?

62
00:03:43.716 --> 00:03:45.622
Use the base verb after could.

63
00:03:46.433 --> 00:03:49.051
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:49.867 --> 00:03:51.344
Polite Questions.

65
00:03:51.644 --> 00:03:53.469
Excuse me, may I come in?

66
00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.466
Could you open the window, please?

67
00:03:57.467 --> 00:03:58.955
Can I borrow your pen?

68
00:03:59.967 --> 00:04:02.445
Sure, here you are. Thank you!

69
00:04:03.433 --> 00:04:06.083
Sorry, I can't help now, but I can help later.

70
00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:11.424
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:12.283 --> 00:04:14.051
blank I come in, please?

72
00:04:14.351 --> 00:04:17.354
A, May. B, Do. C, Am.

73
00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.644
The answer is A: May.

74
00:04:23.783 --> 00:04:25.574
blank you help me, please?

75
00:04:25.874 --> 00:04:28.958
A, Could. B, Do. C, Must.

76
00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.383
The answer is A: Could.

77
00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.424
Can I sit here? blank

78
00:04:37.724 --> 00:04:41.761
A, Sure.. B, Yes, I sit.. C, Sit I can..

79
00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.195
The answer is A: Sure..

80
00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.966
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:50.266 --> 00:04:54.756
A, Could you to help me?. B, Could you help me?. C, Could you helping me?.

82
00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.776
The answer is B: Could you help me?.

83
00:05:01.917 --> 00:05:05.170
According to the reading, what does the writer want to borrow?

84
00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:08.589
A, a pen. B, a book. C, a bike.

85
00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:14.412
The answer is A: a pen.

86
00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.659
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:19.517 --> 00:05:22.039
Ask your teacher a polite question with 'could'.

88
00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.350
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:46.082
Excuse me, could you repeat the question, please? I would like to understand it better. I use could because it is polite. I add please at the end, and I say thank you when the teacher helps me.

90
00:05:46.382 --> 00:05:48.056
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:55.794
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and requests: can and could and may plus subject plus base verb.

92
00:05:56.094 --> 00:05:59.535
Today's value is politeness. Say please and thank you.

93
00:05:59.835 --> 00:06:02.615
See you in Unit thirty-nine. Goodbye!

94
00:06:02.915 --> 00:06:05.974
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

